Description: Tools for dynamic modeling and parameter estimation in ordinary
    differential equation (ODE) models of reaction networks. Models are built
    symbolically and compiled to C/C++ with first- and second-order
    sensitivities. Prediction, observation and objective functions are
    composable function objects that carry symbolic derivatives, following the
    paradigm that derivative information should be used for optimization
    whenever possible. Beyond single-model fitting via trust-region
    optimization, multi-start search and profile-likelihood identifiability
    analysis, the package supports nonlinear mixed-effects (population) fitting
    (FOCEI, adaptive sparse-grid Gauss-Hermite quadrature, Laplace-EM and
    stochastic-approximation EM), Bayesian Markov chain Monte Carlo, structural
    identifiability via symmetry detection, symbolic steady states, and
    PEtab / SBML import and export.
